# Forward mode in the tunables of the frame evaluator with particle mesh
# Ewald (D389, #726): the tangent of the gradient in
# the positions in the charges of every particle against torch-pme (Loche
# et al., J. Chem. Phys. 162, 142501 (2025)), the half difference of its
# gradient at the charges shifted by the tangent and back (exact: quadratic
# in the charges), at the grids 64 and 128, within three times what each
# program changes by between them (Inputs/python_frame_gradients.py).
#
# REQUIRES: python-api, torch, torchpme, cuda
#
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_jvp.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torchpme GPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_jvp.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torchpme GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the dipeptide in water, 1168 particles: the tangent of G in the charges against torch-pme, grid 64
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the dipeptide in water: the same at 128 points
# CHECK: torchpme passed
